# SABOTAGE: E7 four-audit-tiers-disjoint (ADR-040 §6/§7.4; T119).
# A versioned + impersonated write must produce BOTH an E7 `<Resource>.Version` row AND
# EXACTLY ONE §6.6 `impersonation_write` governance aud_event (for the source write) — never
# a second aud_event for the version-row create itself. ash_paper_trail's CreateNewVersion
# creates the Version row INSIDE the source action's transaction carrying the SAME (operator)
# actor, so without a guard the global Samen.Audit.ImpersonationWrite change would fire AGAIN
# on the version resource, double-counting into the governance tier and collapsing the
# tier-disjointness invariant. Samen.Audit.ImpersonationWrite.version_resource?/1 is that
# guard (it no-ops the audit on any generated version module, detected via resource_version?/0).
# This sabotage disables the guard, so an impersonated versioned write self-audits its version
# create and the tiers-disjoint RED test sees TWO impersonation_write rows instead of one.
# The named RED test MUST fail — proving the "exactly one governance row per impersonated
# write" assertion is not a tautology.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/versioned_change_log_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a versioned + impersonated write produces BOTH a Version row AND exactly one impersonation_write aud_event
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/audit/impersonation_write.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/audit/impersonation_write.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/audit/impersonation_write.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/audit/impersonation_write.ex
@@ -163,6 +163,9 @@
   end

   # ash_paper_trail stamps every generated version module with `resource_version?/0`.
+  # SABOTAGE (T119 §7.4 tiers-disjoint): disable the version-resource guard so an
+  # impersonated versioned write ALSO self-audits its Version-row create (=> 2 rows).
+  defp version_resource?(_resource) when 1 == 1, do: false
   defp version_resource?(resource) do
     is_atom(resource) and function_exported?(resource, :resource_version?, 0) and
       resource.resource_version?()
